.Dd October 31, 2026
.Dt SW_VERS 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm sw_vers
.Nd print the operating system's version
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl productName | Fl productVersion | Fl buildVersion
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With no option,
.Nm
prints the system's name and release, and the version of the kernel under
it, as in
.Dl Minkar 19.6.0 (kernel Darwin 19.6.0)
.Pp
The options print one value each, from
.Pa /System/Library/CoreServices/SystemVersion.plist :
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl productName
The system's name
.Pq Li ProductName .
.It Fl productVersion
The version of the Cocoa API the system is compatible with
.Pq Li ProductVersion ,
such as 10.15 for API 19: what programs and scripts compare to know which
interfaces they can use. It is not the release.
.It Fl buildVersion
The build
.Pq Li ProductBuildVersion .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr uname 1
